Keeps this directory in git when it is otherwise empty.

pubspec.yaml declares `assets/fonts/` as an asset directory, and Flutter fails
the build when a declared directory does not exist. Git does not track empty
directories, so without this file a checkout with no fonts breaks the build.

Since v0.5.0 the directory is NOT empty: IBMPlexSans-Regular.ttf and
IBMPlexSans-Bold.ttf are committed (SIL Open Font License, see
LICENSE-IBMPlexSans.txt). They do two jobs.

1. PDF reports. lib/report/report_fonts.dart loads them and reports the exact
   character coverage; without them dart_pdf falls back to the built-in
   Helvetica, which covers Latin-1 (including the `µ` of `µs`) but not
   arbitrary clinical notes, and the app warns on every export that replaced a
   character.

2. Documentation screenshots. flutter_tester ships no fonts at all, so
   test/docs/screenshots_test.dart registers these; without them it falls back
   to a host system font and the committed PNGs stop being reproducible between
   machines and CI.
